# Line-ending policy — added 2026-08-17.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS
# Four files come from John Schuler and are CRLF; everything we wrote is LF.
# On 2026-08-13 our edits silently flipped three of them, inflating
# functions4.jl's diff from 62 lines to 1,122. The flip was invisible until
# `git diff --stat` was compared against `git diff --stat -w`.
#
# WHY `-text` AND NOT `text eol=crlf`
# `-text` tells git to perform NO end-of-line conversion on these paths, so the
# bytes already committed stay exactly as they are. `text eol=crlf` would be the
# more aggressive fix — it makes git normalise to LF in the index, which would
# render future flips invisible — but it requires a one-time
# `git add --renormalize`, producing precisely the whole-file diff on
# functions4.jl that open item 12 (sending Schuler our changes) needs to avoid.
# Revisit after that diff has been sent and accepted.
#
# THIS DOES NOT STOP AN EDITOR FROM REWRITING LINE ENDINGS.
# It only stops git from doing conversions of its own, so what you see in
# `git diff` is the truth. The detector is still mandatory before committing
# anything that touches these four files:
#
#     git diff --stat            # if this disagrees with the next line,
#     git diff --stat -w         # an EOL flip has happened — fix before staging
#
# Schuler's files — published model code, CRLF, do not convert.
functions4.jl    -text
finMain0001.jl   -text
parameterGen.jl  -text
objects.jl       -text

# restart.jl is also CRLF-origin and is not currently wired in
# (finMain0001.jl:90); pin it so it does not drift while dormant.
restart.jl       -text
